      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10265063::page::001"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Undoped MnNiSi exhibits a significant magnetocaloric effect.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Undoped MnNiSi has limited mechanical robustness, including brittleness.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed intervention replaces approximately 10–20% of the Mn sites with Fe to form Mn1-xFexNiSi with x approximately 0.1–0.2.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Doping or isostructural substitution can be used to tailor magnetostructural coupling in MM'X magnetocaloric compounds.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10265063::page::001"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "Fe substitution will modify the local bonding environment in Mn1-xFexNiSi.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Fe substitution will modify grain-boundary characteristics.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Fe-induced bonding and grain-boundary changes will improve lattice stability and ductility.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Fe doping introduces controlled chemical disorder that stabilizes the lattice.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Fe-induced chemical disorder will reduce microcrack formation and enhance ductility.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Fe substitution at x approximately 0.1–0.2 will not disrupt the magnetostructural transition required for the large magnetocaloric effect.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10265063::page::001"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Samples with x approximately 0.1–0.2 will have greater fracture toughness and ductility than undoped MnNiSi.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Samples with x approximately 0.1–0.2 will retain a magnetic entropy change comparable to undoped MnNiSi.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10265063::page::001"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Above approximately 20–30% Fe substitution, structural and magnetic transition temperatures may be adversely affected.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Adverse changes in transition temperatures above approximately 20–30% Fe substitution may diminish the magnetocaloric effect.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed comparison uses identically processed x = 0, 0.1, 0.2, and 0.3 samples tested for mechanical, magnetocaloric, and microstructural properties.",
      "field": "falsification_experiment.design",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The hypothesis is falsified if x = 0.1–0.2 samples fail to show a statistically significant mechanical improvement while maintaining magnetocaloric performance within experimental uncertainty of the undoped baseline.",
      "field": "falsification_experiment.falsification_rule",
      "needs_support": false,
